# XDK C# / .NET SDK

Official C# / .NET SDK for the X API v2 (.NET 8+, zero external runtime dependencies).

## Installation

```bash
dotnet add package Xdk --version {{ version }}
```

## Quick Start

```csharp
using Xdk;
using Xdk.Models;

var client = new XClient(new XClientOptions
{
    BearerToken = Environment.GetEnvironmentVariable("X_BEARER_TOKEN")
});

var response = await client.Users.GetByUsernameAsync("XDevelopers");
Console.WriteLine(response.Data);
```

## Authentication

- **Bearer Token (App-Only)**: `new XClient(new XClientOptions { BearerToken = "..." })`
- **OAuth 2.0 PKCE & Refresh**: `OAuth2Pkce` + `new XClient(new XClientOptions { OAuth2 = oauth2 })`
- **OAuth 1.0a User Context**: `OAuth1` + `new XClient(new XClientOptions { OAuth1 = oauth1 })`

## Pagination & Streaming

- Paginated endpoints expose `*Pages(...)` returning `Paginator<T>` (`IAsyncEnumerable<T>`), enabling `await foreach (var page in client.Users.GetFollowersPages(id))`.
- Streaming endpoints return `EventStream<T>` (`IAsyncEnumerable<T>` and `IAsyncDisposable`) with incremental UTF-8 line decoding and exponential backoff reconnection.

## Examples & Continuous Canary

- **Runnable Use-Case Examples**: See [`examples/Xdk.Examples/`](examples/Xdk.Examples/) for end-to-end runnable workflows covering Posts, Search, Users, Bookmarks, Filtered & Sample Streaming, Chunked Media Upload, Direct Messages & XChat, Lists, Spaces, Communities, Community Notes, Trends, News, Webhooks, Compliance, Usage, and OAuth 1.0a / 2.0 PKCE.
- **Continuous Canary Runner**: Run `dotnet run --project examples/Xdk.Examples -- --canary --once` (or `--canary --daemon --port 8791` for an always-on `/health`, `/status`, and `/metrics` probe server against the built-in X API simulator or live `X_BEARER_TOKEN`).
